{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-75369",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we decompose all of the terms into their various factors. The $12(x-1)$ in the numerator becomes $2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3\\cdot (x-1),$ and the $15x$ in the denominator becomes $3\\cdot 5\\cdot x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12(x-1)}{15x}=\\frac{2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3\\cdot (x-1)}{3\\cdot 5\\cdot x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel out all the pairs of common factors in the numerator and denominator. In this case, there is one pair of $3$'s.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3\\cdot (x-1)}{3\\cdot 5\\cdot x} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot 2\\cdot \\cancel{3}\\cdot (x-1)}{\\cancel{3}\\cdot 5\\cdot x} & = \\\\ \\frac{2\\cdot 2\\cdot (x-1)}{5\\cdot x} & = \\\\ \\frac{4(x-1)}{5x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the expression simplifies to $\\frac{4(x-1)}{5x}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
